# 62. Product Backlog

---

# 1. Purpose

The Product Backlog is the authoritative implementation planning document for the Loyalty Platform.

Unlike a traditional Scrum backlog, this backlog is designed to support both human engineering teams and AI implementation agents.

Its objectives are to:

- transform Blueprint decisions into implementation work;
- provide a stable planning structure;
- support parallel development;
- minimize implementation ambiguity;
- define implementation ownership;
- support dependency management;
- standardize AI task generation;
- provide complete implementation traceability.

This document does not replace the Blueprint.

The Blueprint defines **what the system is**.

The Product Backlog defines **how implementation work is organized**.

---

# 2. Scope

The Product Backlog contains only implementation work.

It does not contain:

- product ideas;
- brainstorming;
- architecture discussions;
- rejected proposals;
- future roadmap concepts.

Every backlog item must be traceable to an approved Blueprint decision.

---

# 3. Backlog Principles

The Product Backlog follows these principles:

- Blueprint First
- Business Value First
- Small Implementation Units
- Clear Ownership
- Dependency Transparency
- AI-Friendly Context
- Independent Verification
- Incremental Delivery
- Reversible Implementation
- Complete Traceability

No backlog item may introduce new Product Decisions.

---

# 4. Backlog Hierarchy

Implementation work is organized using the following hierarchy:

```
Vision
    ↓
Epic
    ↓
Capability
    ↓
Feature
    ↓
Task
    ↓
Subtask
```

Each level exists to reduce planning complexity.

Only Tasks are assigned directly to implementation agents.

